{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789479621,"nonce":"lhmfMljVph7EQJdQaRqsWWwpdNo=","title":"b4 review tui: reply editor buffer omits under-the-cut (\"---\") notes, no way to comment on them","message":"Reported by K while trying to reply to Brigham Campbell's patch:\n\n  [PATCH b4] ez: include mbox \"From \" line in auto-to-cc input\n  https://lore.kernel.org/tools/20260914-mbox-from-auto-to-cc-v1-1-fbf0c3fbd460@brighamcampbell.com/\n  Message-ID: \u003c20260914-mbox-from-auto-to-cc-v1-1-fbf0c3fbd460@brighamcampbell.com\u003e\n\nThat patch has rationale under the cut (after Signed-off-by, before the\ndiffstat) explaining why the author thinks b4 should use git format-patch\ninstead of hand-formatting patches. It shows up in the read-only content\nviewer but there is no way to reply to it: opening the reply editor jumps\nstraight from the commit message to the quoted diff, skipping it entirely.\n\nCode path\n---------\n\n- ``create_review_branch()`` (src/b4/review/_review.py:355-386) does capture\n  this text: it splits each patch's basement on ``b4.DIFF_RE`` and stores\n  everything before the diff as ``pmeta['basement']`` in the tracking JSON\n  committed at the tip of the review branch.\n- The content viewer (src/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:687-695) reads\n  ``patch_meta.get('basement', '')`` and renders it read-only under a\n  ``---`` divider, dim-styled, with no line numbers tracked.\n- The reply editor (``action_edit_reply``,\n  src/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:1314-1369) builds its buffer from two\n  sources only: ``git show --format=%B --no-patch \u003csha\u003e`` for the commit\n  message (which itself already stops at the original ``---`` -- that's\n  where the applied commit's message ends) and ``git diff`` for the hunks.\n  Both go through ``_render_quoted_diff_with_comments()``\n  (src/b4/review/_review.py:1980-2100), which only knows how to quote two\n  things: commit-message lines (keyed ``(':message', lineno)``) and diff\n  hunk lines (keyed ``(file, lineno)``). ``pmeta['basement']`` is never\n  passed to it.\n\nCause\n-----\n\nThe basement text is captured and displayed, but was never wired into the\nreply path: no anchor scheme (``comment_map`` key) exists for it, and\n``action_edit_reply`` never reads ``patch_meta.get('basement')`` when\nassembling ``editor_text``. It is functionally a third kind of quotable\nregion (alongside commit message and diff) that only got a renderer, not a\nreply target.","files":null}]}